      "explanation": "First, \\(x\\ne0\\), because \\(x/2\\) is a denominator. Simplifying the two compound fractions gives\n\\[\n\\frac{x/4}{2}=\\frac{x}{8},\\qquad\n\\frac{4}{x/2}=4\\cdot\\frac{2}{x}=\\frac{8}{x}.\n\\]\nThus the equation is \\(x/8=8/x\\). Multiplying both sides by \\(8x\\), which is nonzero, removes the denominators:\n\\[\nx^2=64.\n\\]\nThe two square roots of \\(64\\) are \\(8\\) and \\(-8\\). In the original equation, both sides equal \\(1\\) when \\(x=8\\), and both equal \\(-1\\) when \\(x=-8\\). Therefore \\(\\boxed{x=\\pm8}\\), choice E.",
